# SABOTAGE: ADR-048 §8 P1 / CF-22 (Gap D) — the ingress ORDER in
# `Samen.AI.Agent.Compaction.scrub/1` is SWAPPED: `Ingress.sanitize/1` now runs BEFORE
# `Secrets.redact/1`, instead of the pinned order (`compaction.ex:118`,
# `summary |> Secrets.redact() |> Ingress.sanitize()`). A labeled secret whose value is
# separated from its label by U+200B (a `\p{Cf}` format character) survives: redact-first
# treats U+200B as inside the label/value gap and collapses the whole span in one match;
# sanitize-first replaces U+200B with the eleven-LETTER marker `[neutralized]`, which ENDS
# that non-language gap before `Secrets.redact/1` ever sees it, so the credential is left in
# cleartext. This is the ORDER attack, distinct from `314-t219-...-dropped.patch`, which
# DROPS both lanes rather than swapping them.
#
# Flips the new P1 ORDER red added for CF-22. The three pre-existing P1 arms (the two
# `P1: RED —` neutralization arms and the `P1: POSITIVE CONTROL —` prose arm) stay GREEN
# under this swap: their `@poisoned_summary` fixture carries an injected instruction matched
# by a `\p{L}`-only phrase pattern and a contiguous vendor-prefixed key matched by a
# contiguous-printable pattern, and neither class depends on label/value adjacency — so
# neither lane's order matters to them. That is the literal restatement of CF-22: the order
# bug is real but none of P1's existing coverage could see it before this node's new arm.
#
# Touches compaction.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_summarizer_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: P1: RED — a LABELED SECRET separated from its label by U+200B is REDACTED in the persisted llm_view under the correct ingress ORDER (Secrets.redact/1 runs before Ingress.sanitize/1)
